 "result": "The subagent's line number was slightly off. The failing call is in `SignedCookieSessionInterface.save_session` in `src/tessel/sessions.py`, not at line 374.\n\n- **Main call (the one the tests hit):** the `response.set_cookie(...)` call that begins at `sessions.py:372` and passes `partitioned=partitioned` at **line 382**. This is the path that writes the session cookie.\n- **Same kwarg, delete path:** the `response.delete_cookie(...)` call just above passes `partitioned=partitioned` at **line 361**. It runs when the session is emptied.\n\nThe argument installed Werkzeug 3.0.3 rejects is **`partitioned`**. `set_cookie()` and `delete_cookie()` only gained that keyword in 3.1, so 3.0.3 raises `TypeError: set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The value comes from `get_cookie_partitioned(app)` (defined at line 215, assigned at line 344).\n\nI confirmed the lines by reading the source. I did not re-run a test to see the exact `TypeError` text, so that message is inferred from the subagent's report.",
